# Energy dashboard panel

Full-page kind `energy_dashboard` (Other tiles). Charts are **player-native Compose** over a Remote Compose `componentId` hole. The existing `energy` “Energy now” live power-flow tile is unchanged.

## Wiring

- Catalogue: `energy_dashboard` in `_kinds.yaml` (`sizes: [full]`, `card: none`).
- Editor: `OTHER_TILE_KINDS`, `TileDrawer` edge-to-edge, `GridMockup` static mock.
- Server: `Tile.edgeToEdge` + `Tiles.kt` → `energyDashboardPanel` (`render/panels/energydashboard/`). Stub RC hole uses `Role.PAGE`.
- Stub RC page shows “Update the tablet app…”; capable players overlay `EnergyDashboardScreen`.
- Data: `EnergyDashboardRepository` (`energy/get_prefs`, `recorder/statistics_during_period`, `energy/fossil_energy_consumption`) + area map for Sankey. Prefetch in `RenderDataRepository.forScreen` when the kind is present.
- Period UI: `EnergyDashboardUiStore` + verbs `energy_dash_prev` / `next` / `now` / `period` → `EnergyDashboardActions` → Rebuild.
- Protocol: `CAPABILITY_ENERGY_DASHBOARD`, `ServerMessage.EnergyDashboard` (page, componentId, series, totals, sankey, `theme`, …). `Document.energyPages` lists MAIN pages that have a dashboard (null = older add-on).
- Player: Hello capability; `RemoteScreenState.energyDashboards` / `playingEnergyDashboard`; `DocumentOverlays` places `EnergyDashboardScreen` on MAIN page bounds. Keep the overlay across document rebuilds until a matching-revision payload arrives (see `session-document-rebuild-context.mdc`).
- `SessionMedia.sendEnergyDashboard` is async after the document; do not clear the previous dashboard on `withDocument` or the charts blink.

## Theme colours (from the server)

Chrome is **not** the player’s `RemoteScreensTheme` Material scheme. The add-on resolves the screen `Palette` and sends it on the message:

- `SessionMedia`: `theme = shown.renderedDoc.docContext.palette.toEnergyTheme()` → `EnergyDashboardTheme` (`page`, `card`, `ink`, `inkDim`, `accent`, `track` from `Role.PAGE` / `CARD` / `INK` / `INK_DIM` / `ACCENT` / `TRACK`).
- Player: `message.theme.toEnergyColors()` + `LocalEnergyColors` (`EnergyColors.kt`). Electricity columns, gauge arc, “Now”, period bar, cards, and page background read that local.
- Low-carbon green, grid blue, and per-device / Sankey categorical colours stay fixed so series stay distinct.
- Defaults on `EnergyDashboardTheme` are the previous hardcoded dark/blue values. An older add-on that omits `theme` (or a tablet before this player) still paints that dashboard. **Redeploy the add-on** before expecting teal accent parity with the RC nav on a live tablet.

## Charts

Player-native UI split:

- `EnergyDashboardScreen.kt` — page shell + period bar + `CompositionLocalProvider`.
- `EnergyDashboardCards.kt` — totals, rank, distribution, gauge, Sankey, electricity/devices cards.
- `EnergyDashboardCharts.kt` — Vico column charts (electricity + stacked devices) with shared thickness/spacing and preview-safe synchronous models. `remember(series)` so equal data does not reset the model.

Compose rows/Canvas cover rank, gauge, distribution, and Sankey. Every UI composable has a same-file `@Preview`. Vico samples use ≈24 day buckets so content-zoom does not fatten columns. Devices detail charts when `series` is non-empty (labels optional).

Vico deps: `compose` / `core` / `compose-m3` (see player `build.gradle.kts`).

